  "synthesis": {
    "overnight_summary": "Gold slipped 0.6% on Monday to ~$4,169 as oil at a 4-week high kept December Fed-hike odds near 88% and the dollar held near an 18-month high, then recovered to ~$4,184 in Asia (+$15) amid Houthi attacks on Riyadh airport and Iran's refusal to talk on Hormuz. For MCX the rupee dominates again: RBI widened its rupee defence and sold dollars, and USD/INR opened at 95.17 (+60 paise), worth about Rs -913 against +Rs 548 from COMEX. Model fair open was Rs 149,178 vs Monday's close of 1,49,543; MCX actually opened at 1,49,653, Rs 475 rich, and drifted to ~1,49,470 by 11:40 IST. Expect a heavy, range-bound session below 1,50,000 ahead of Wednesday's US CPI, with the rupee the swing factor.",
